<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  High-frequency sportsbook capture near tip-off, every 5 minutes.

  Exists to answer ONE question from MODELING_FINDINGS.md: when Polymarket
  moves, is the book's old price still available? Our routine captures are
  60.1 minutes apart and the follow-through lands inside that gap, so the
  economics of the cross-venue lead cannot currently be tested at all.

  Installed by scripts/install-market-sync.sh.

  5 minutes looks aggressive and is not, because the command gates itself:
  it spends ZERO requests unless a game is inside the window AND has enough
  Polymarket activity to produce the move being studied. Off-season, an
  empty afternoon, or a slate nobody trades all cost nothing. On a WNBA
  game day the real spend is roughly 6 hours x 12 per hour = ~72 requests.

  Read-only price capture. There is no order placement anywhere in this
  codebase and none should be added (ROADMAP.md non-goals).

  Runs HERE rather than on the capture host, unlike the Kalshi/Polymarket
  recorder. That one records feeds whose quotes are unrecoverable; this one
  reads a paid API with a shared quota, and pointing two machines at the
  same key would double the burn while halving nobody's uncertainty.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.ostepan.wnba-odds-focused</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/zsh</string>
        <string>-lc</string>
        <string>cd PLACEHOLDER_REPO &amp;&amp; uv run wnba-engine capture-odds-focused</string>
    </array>

    <!-- 5 minutes. -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>

    <!-- Deliberately NOT RunAtLoad. Unlike the capture agent, a missed
         window here is not lost data - the routine hourly snapshot still
         runs - so there is no reason to fire an extra request on every
         reload while iterating on the plist. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>PLACEHOLDER_HOME/wnba-market-capture/logs/odds-focused.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>PLACEHOLDER_HOME/wnba-market-capture/logs/odds-focused.log</string>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>PLACEHOLDER_REPO</string>
</dict>
</plist>
